I'm the boss of myself."

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.860
And that means that I take responsibility

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.210
for my decision making.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.540
For if I, you know, if
I'm in a down spirit,

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.580
it's up to me to pick myself up.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:45.413
- Yeah.

00:08:45.413 --> 00:08:47.190
- So I start getting into my songwriting.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.990
'Cause that's what I do when I get bored

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.153
or when I'm too isolated.

00:08:50.153 --> 00:08:52.200
- Me too.
- And I, right?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.877
- Yeah, that's where I work it out.

00:08:53.877 --> 00:08:55.590
- Personally, that's where
you work it out, it's therapy.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.477
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So I'm thinking,

00:08:57.477 --> 00:09:00.277
"Okay, I'm gonna just write
myself into a better spirit."

00:09:00.277 --> 00:09:01.750
- That's beautiful.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.870
- I'm gonna write songs
that make me wanna dance

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:04.950
and make me feel happy.
(audience cheers)

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:05.940
- Yeah.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.410
You have a song I wanna talk about.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.000
It's called "Inhale, Exhale".

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.260
- Yeah.
- What's that about?

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:11.099
What a cool title.

00:09:11.099 --> 00:09:12.875
What a cool vibe, yeah.

00:09:12.875 --> 00:09:14.550
- "Inhale, Exhale".

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.006
I affectionately call the song "Air".

00:09:16.006 --> 00:09:19.590
With everyone suffering from, you know,

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.457
the Covid is such a respiratory, you know,

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.550
infection that really can take
your life very, very quickly.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.912
I had a bad bout with it.

00:09:30.912 --> 00:09:32.670
I won't go into it,

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.250
but when I was released from the hospital,

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.829
the first thing I did was
write down a list of things

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:41.671
that air gives us.

00:09:41.671 --> 00:09:43.770
Obviously life.
- Yeah.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:47.130
- But I'm thinking,
"Okay, cheer yourself up.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.952
What does air give us
that is very celebratory?"

00:09:49.952 --> 00:09:53.837
So I'm thinking, champagne
bubbles, balloons, you know-

00:09:53.837 --> 00:09:55.392
- I love where your brain went.

00:09:55.392 --> 00:09:56.395
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:57.392
- Sailing though, too.

00:09:57.392 --> 00:09:59.915
It's like, you know,
with the air we can sail,

00:09:59.915 --> 00:10:02.640
we can sail, we can
fly, we can fly a kite.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:06.960
We have all these lovely
things to celebrate about air.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.090
And of course, like I said,
you know, life itself.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.300
So I wrote the song, what are you gonna do

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.537
without that air, you know?

00:10:13.537 --> 00:10:15.030
"Inhale, Exhale".

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:17.070
So that's the most
inspired song on the album.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.120
- Yeah, I love that though,

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.050
when it comes from real life

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.949
and then you come up with this
completely different concept

00:10:20.949 --> 00:10:22.440
off of that one moment.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.030
- Well, because I didn't
wanna look back on it.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.251
I'm like, "Okay, whew, I'm through it.

00:10:26.251 --> 00:10:29.211
Write a happy song about
surviving it and celebrate."

00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:30.510
- I love that you do that.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:31.343
We are so different.

00:10:31.343 --> 00:10:33.211
So I'm gonna try what you do.

00:10:33.211 --> 00:10:35.872
I usually write when I'm
sad, and I get it out.

00:10:35.872 --> 00:10:38.880
I've never written to become happy,

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.392
which is maybe the larger issue.

00:10:41.392 --> 00:10:42.411
(Shania laughs)

00:10:42.411 --> 00:10:45.030
I'm finding in this interview.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:48.090
But that's a very clever
thing to use your gift for,

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.800
like to write, to be happy.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.660
Usually I'm writing just to get it out.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.460
I guess I become happy
after getting it out,

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.370
but like I've never had
the mentality of that.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.203
Anyway, it's cool.

00:10:57.203 --> 00:10:58.320
- No, but it's a great fit.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.429
Song writing is venting, of course.

00:10:59.429 --> 00:11:01.350
That's a great place to vent writing.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.293
- Yeah.

00:11:02.293 --> 00:11:03.333
- [Shania] You know, but
I mean, even writing-

00:11:03.333 --> 00:11:04.432
- [Kelly] Welcome to my albums.

00:11:04.432 --> 00:11:05.447
(group laughs)

00:11:05.447 --> 00:11:07.710
- But writing songs, I do
it as an exercise also.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:08.730
And to challenge myself.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.650
So I, of course, I write lots of songs

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.210
that are very melancholy, very dark.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.213
If I'm really upset and mad,
I put it all in the song.

00:11:14.213 --> 00:11:15.232
- Yeah.

00:11:15.232 --> 00:11:17.400
- But then I go back to it later,

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.980
and I turn it around, just
like a writing exercise.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.160
I just turn it around and now
I make it just like you would

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.629
if putting a song in first-person

00:11:24.629 --> 00:11:25.649
or third-person or whatever.

00:11:25.649 --> 00:11:26.651
- You find the light in it.

00:11:26.651 --> 00:11:27.653
Yeah, that's cool.

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:28.651
- [Shania] Yeah.
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:11:28.651 --> 00:11:29.653
- Finding the upside of everything.

00:11:29.653 --> 00:11:30.672
- I know.

00:11:30.672 --> 00:11:31.505
So it can be difficult,

00:11:31.505 --> 00:11:32.693
but I hear that you're pretty competitive.

00:11:32.693 --> 00:11:34.860
How about a game after the break?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:35.693
- Oh, yeah.
- [Kelly] Are you down?

00:11:35.693 --> 00:11:37.365
- [Shania] I'm up, I'm
down, I'm up, I'm up for it.

00:11:37.365 --> 00:11:38.566
- Okay, I just wanna, I'm
up and I'm down for it.

00:11:38.566 --> 00:11:39.569
(both laugh)

00:11:39.569 --> 00:11:41.741
I just wanna beat you at this game.

00:11:41.741 --> 00:11:42.574
(Kelly laughs)
(audience claps)

